{
  "requirement": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion_trait`\n\n[`Criterion::Ok`](../../../rustdocs/trust_but_verify/graph/trait.Criterion.html#associatedtype.Ok)\ndefines the criterion's completed answer:\n\n```rust,ignore\nuse serde::{Serialize, de::DeserializeOwned};\n\npub trait Criterion<D: Domain>: Send + Sized {\n    // ...\n\n    /// The completed answer, including any negative assessment.\n    /// Its Serde JSON representation must reconstruct the completed answer.\n    type Ok: Serialize + DeserializeOwned + Send;\n\n    // ...\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject requires `Criterion::Ok` to be `Serialize + DeserializeOwned + Send`. It also requires the answer to include any negative assessment, and its Serde JSON form to reconstruct the completed answer. I derived these obligations from the requirement text. I did not read the implementation or the test helpers (`Review`, `Cell`, `persist`, `answer`), so I am assuming they behave as their names and use suggest.\n\n- **Negative answers survive a JSON round trip.**\n  - `tests/contracts.rs#fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]` verifies a negative answer, `answer(false, \"missing edge case\")`.\n  - It stores the value, then reloads it. It asserts the loaded `output()` and `into_output()` equal the original negative answer.\n  - It also asserts the stored JSON record is `{\"satisfied\":false,\"details\":[\"missing edge case\"]}`.\n  - A representation that dropped the negative state or its details would fail these assertions.\n- **Other answer shapes round-trip.** The same test round-trips a `Vec<String>` answer (`structure`). It also round-trips a unit `()` answer, which is stored as `json!(null)` and reloaded. The structured, collection and unit shapes all reconstruct.\n- **Send without Sync.** `validation_and_answer_need_send_without_sync` uses a `Cell<u32>` answer. It is `Send` but not `Sync`, and the test runs it through `send(...)` on verify, store, load and refresh. It asserts the reloaded value is 17 and the refreshed value is 23, so the answer type compiles and round-trips under the `Send`-only bound.\n- **Serialize and DeserializeOwned.** The store and load paths in both tests exercise these bounds, and the compiled generic bounds enforce them.\n\nI found no input class or assertion that would let a violation pass unnoticed. Both tests carry `{test}` references to the subject, so there is no marking gap.",
